<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    French translation.

    It was the application's source language until the project stopped being
    a Lille one; the strings are still written first here in spirit, since the
    interface's tone was set in French, but `values/` is what Android falls
    back on and English is what it holds.

    Rules, the same as everywhere: positional placeholders, <plurals> for
    anything that agrees, and the `name` attributes left untouched.

    The typography is French: the apostrophe is ’ and not the straight quote,
    which is why nothing here is escaped, and `?`, `!`, `;`, `:` and the inside
    of « » carry a non-breaking space. See CONTRIBUTING.md.
-->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

